A '''zoglin''' is an [[undead]] [[hostile mob]] created when a [[hoglin]] is out of the [[Nether]] for too long. It never retreats or flees, and attacks [[player]]s and almost all non-zoglin [[mob]]s indiscriminately, using the same tusk attack as its non-zombified counterpart.

== Spawning ==
Zoglins spawn when a [[hoglin]] has been out of the [[Nether]] for {{convert|300|ticks|seconds}}. For their first 10 seconds after zombification, they get the [[Nausea]] effect{{only|java|short=1}}<ref>This does not happen in Bedrock Edition due to {{bug|MCPE-70866}}.</ref>. This nausea effect is cosmetic and does not affect its behavior.

Like most [[hostile]] mobs, zoglins despawn when the [[difficulty]] is changed to [[Peaceful]].

